    {
      "step": "rule-selection: an auth payload with an unknown field",
      "cause": "soroban-sdk 28 (carried into 29) unpacks a #[contracttype] struct leniently: a map key the struct does not define is ignored instead of failing the conversion (soroban-sdk _migrating::v28_contracttype_unpacking). The account's __check_auth takes its signature as stellar-accounts' AuthPayload, so an auth entry whose signature map carries an extra key, which soroban-sdk 27 refused while decoding (WasmVm InvalidAction), now decodes and is checked like the same payload without the key: the signers and context_rule_ids it does carry are verified as before, and the call is authorized. No other step differs.",
