      "step": "recovery-removal: owner removes recovery",
      "cause": "soroban-sdk 28 (carried into 29) publishes a #[contractevent] whose data format is a map without its void fields (soroban-sdk _migrating::v28_contractevent_packing). perch-recovery's EpochAdvanced { account, epoch, config_hash: Option<BytesN<32>> } is published with config_hash None when an account's recovery configuration is removed; its data map now holds only epoch, where soroban-sdk 27 also carried config_hash as void. Readers that treat an absent config_hash as None see the same event. The same applies to any Perch event with an Option field that is None; EpochAdvanced is the only one with such a field.",
